This software is **not** legal advice.

Compliance Grid produces structured, cited summaries of regulatory
obligations. Every obligation carries a `source_refs[]` pointer to
the underlying document it was extracted from. The system is designed
to *cite, never invent* — but extraction is AI-assisted and operators
who rely on outputs for compliance decisions must verify against the
cited sources.

The maintainers and contributors of Compliance Grid disclaim all
liability for compliance decisions made on the basis of outputs from
this software. Per D13 (locked decision): this is decision-support
with mandatory source citations and explicit freshness/confidence
labels. It is not authoritative legal advice.

